; link/pop_boot.link — the STAGE-1 LOADER (P4.46).
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY $0E00, AND WHY IT IS A FLOOR RATHER THAN A PREFERENCE
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DECB's own storage sits below: DBUF0 $0600, DBUF1 $0700, the FAT $0800, the FCBs $094A.
; A program loaded under those is written over BY THE LOADER THAT IS LOADING IT, and P3.4
; measured the edge -- $0D00 loads and RUNS with silently damaged data, $0E00 is clean.
; map_overlap_check.py asserts the $0E00 floor on every build for exactly that reason.
;
; ★ THE LOADER IS TRANSIENT AND ITS SPACE IS REUSED. The intro later reads its 4,504-byte
; music player to $0A00..$1B97, straight over this code -- which is correct: by then the
; loader has jumped away and will not be re-entered. Nothing here needs to survive.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THE KERNEL IS LINKED IN AND WHY THAT COSTS NOTHING
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `code` is the same hal_build.o at the same $7900 the intro links. So when the loader
; hands over, the intro finds its kernel ALREADY RESIDENT and never reads one -- the same
; relationship link/pop_scene.link has with the scene, where the staged image's kernel
; segment is dropped because re-reading it while it executes the read would overwrite the
; routine mid-transfer. Here the intro's program is read WITHOUT its kernel segment for the
; same reason, and kernel_identical_check.py is what turns "identical by construction" into
; a checked fact.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE MAP AT LOADER TIME
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;   $0E00-$1FFF   this loader + the screen's patch and palette   (4,608 B available)
;   $2000-$24FA   the intro's program, read here off a raw track
;   $6A00-$6A06   the disk driver's parameter block (DR_VARBASE)
;   $7800-$78FF   trace ring buffer
;   $7900-$7D43   the HAL kernel
;   $7F00         stack top — the same one the intro uses, so the hand-off needs no switch
;   $8000-$FDFF   the draw window; the "loading" screen lives in a framebuffer and
;                 therefore survives the hand-off, which a screen in RAM would not
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

section prog load 0E00
section code load 7900

entry boot_entry
